I must say that I am not a big fan of platformers, but I was attracted by the colossal greed of developers. No, really. Even Bobby Kotick would not have invented a more profitable business scheme. "What kind of business model" - you ask? Well, for stupid people who do not understand the economy, I answer:
Almost without adding anything new developers attracted to the game and get the attention of new customers + 25% of price of the game from old customers + soundtrack DLC + T-shirts, socks, hats, cases for iPhones, notepads, mugs, "artworks" (average price 20-40 $ (proofs:


)) =  additional tens of millions dollars profits.
Questions to the developers: What are you going to sell next? Shampoos, children's chancellery, dishes... or immediately pornographic cartoons? Are you going to start a franchise? Kids cafe, for example.
